        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(brave): resolve env secret refs for search key",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nBrave web search accepted configured API keys, but env-backed SecretRefs in `tools.web.search.apiKey` were not resolved through the shared web-search credential path before falling back to `BRAVE_API_KEY`.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe Brave provider should treat direct API keys, env SecretRefs, and provider fallback env vars consistently with the shared web-search credential contract. This change routes Brave credential resolution through the existing shared resolver instead of duplicating a literal-only read.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can configure Brave web search with an env SecretRef and have it used without live-key tests or custom provider-auth behavior. Existing `BRAVE_API_KEY` fallback behavior remains intact.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Changed `extensions/brave/src/brave-web-search-provider.runtime.ts`.\n- Added a regression in `extensions/brave/src/brave-web-search-provider.test.ts` proving a configured env SecretRef supplies the request auth header ahead of `BRAVE_API_KEY`.\n- Live open-PR conflict scan found no exact overlap on these touched files.\n\n## Proof\n\n- Rebased cleanly onto `upstream/main` at `fbcb7812cb`.\n- `OPENCLAW_HEAVY_CHECK_LOCK_SCOPE=worktree node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/brave/src/brave-web-search-provider.test.ts -- --reporter=verbose`\n- `git diff --check upstream/main..HEAD`\n- Earlier touched-file checks: `pnpm format:check`, `node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs --tsconfig config/tsconfig/oxlint.extensions.json ...`, and Claude autoreview clean after Codex autoreview was blocked by local OpenAI API 401.\n",
        "branch": "llagy007/brave-secretref-env-fallback",
